BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Broken English
DTSTART:20260515T193000Z
DTEND:20260515T212000Z
DTSTAMP:20260515T193000Z
UID:WT5P8IdeEg
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 99 mins (1h39m)\n\nSinger-songwriter and actress Mar
 ianne Faithfull is too big for a simple documentary. Instead\, a theatrica
 l “Department of Not Forgetting” interweaves intimate interviews\, arc
 hival clips\, and newly recorded performances to conjure a holistic unders
 tanding of a career spanning more than half a century.\n\nhttps://www.siff
 .net/festival/broken-english\n\nEstimated start: 12:40
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:En Route To
DTSTART:20260515T220000Z
DTEND:20260515T235500Z
DTSTAMP:20260515T220000Z
UID:Q3X3BNVSir
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 105 mins (1h45m)\n\nA boarding student with a secret
  to hide steals from her hustling roommate to buy black market abortion pi
 lls\; a scheme to reclaim the cash becomes a heartwarming tale of female s
 olidarity in this Berlin-premiered dramedy.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/festiv
 al/en-route-to\n\nEstimated start: 15:10
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jaripeo
DTSTART:20260516T003000Z
DTEND:20260516T015500Z
DTSTAMP:20260516T003000Z
UID:GApPtyeEhL
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 71 mins (1h11m)\n\nSet amid Michoacán’s electrify
 ing bull-riding celebrations\, Jaripeo uncovers queer desire within a fier
 cely hypermasculine world—blending music\, dance\, and intimate stories 
 into a vibrant celebration of sensuality\, joy\, and the freedom to live o
 penly in one’s own skin. Director Efraín Mojica\, Director Rebecca Zwei
 g\, and Producer Sarah Strunin scheduled to attend.\n\nhttps://www.siff.ne
 t/festival/jaripeo\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • Uptown House 3 (Sat 16 May\,
  3:15 PM)\n\nEstimated start: 17:40
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Again Again
DTSTART:20260516T030000Z
DTEND:20260516T045000Z
DTSTAMP:20260516T030000Z
UID:mVrBbkfaUB
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 99 mins (1h39m)\n\nAberdeen-raised director Mia Moor
 e’s debut film\, executive produced by Lilly Wachowski\, is a heady\, ro
 mantic sci-fi starring a trans woman who enters a new day after ten years 
 stuck in “the loop.”Director Mia Moore\, Producer Cliff Noonan\, and E
 xecutive Producer Ian Schrank scheduled to attend.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net
 /festival/again-again\n\nEstimated start: 20:10
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Meadowlarks
DTSTART:20260516T193000Z
DTEND:20260516T212500Z
DTSTAMP:20260516T193000Z
UID:U1U90rHi3o
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 102 mins (1h42m)\n\nIn Meadowlarks\, Tasha Hubbard e
 xplores Sixties Scoop trauma through four reunited siblings in Banff\, bal
 ancing warmth and tension in an intimate\, dialogue-driven story grounded 
 in land and memory. Director Tasha Hubbard (Cree) scheduled to attend.\n\n
 https://www.siff.net/festival/meadowlarks\n\nAlso playing at:\n  • PACCA
 R IMAX Theater at Pacific Science Center (Fri 15 May\, 8:30 PM)\n\nEstimat
 ed start: 12:40
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
